weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cccc4ae9e9f411d5eef265b45b3cf8740aab11ad.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 24 at 1:52PM MDT until October 24 at 4:15PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues along the\nRio Grande and downstream waterways.\n\n* WHERE...Southeastern Mineral County and Rio Grande County...\n\n* WHEN...Until 415 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding will continue along and near the Rio Grande this\nafternoon, especially from near Del Norte to below Monte Vista.\nSeveral roads remain closed and housing areas evacuated due to high\nwater. While many rivers and streams have crested this morning,\nflooding and high flows will continue into the afternoon,\nespecially around Monte Vista.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 143 PM MDT, Water levels along the Rio Grande remain high,\nespecially in the stretch from Del Norte to below Monte Vista,\nalthough the river has crested and levels are forecast to slowly\nfall through the day.\n- Highway 285 between Monte Vista and Center remains closed, and\nHighway 112 between Del Norte and Center is closed as well.\nPlease continue to heed any road closures.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nThe Rio Grande from Del Norte to Monte Vista.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-24T16:15:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Mineral, CO; Rio Grande, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.67667620f7700c972914fc429df0d0c1b76cd6d4.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.67667620f7700c972914fc429df0d0c1b76cd6d4.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 24 at 9:52AM MDT until October 25 at 9:45PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is occurring\n\n* WHERE...Southeastern Rio Grande County in south central Colorado...\nWest Central Alamosa County in southeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 945 PM MDT Sunday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of low lying agricultural areas in Rio Grande\nand Alamosa counties is occurring.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 947 AM MDT, emergency management reported flooding of low\nlying areas in Rio Grande county and in Alamosa county upstream\nof the city of Alamosa.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nMainly rural areas of Southeastern Rio Grande and West Central\nAlamosa Counties.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-25T21:45:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Alamosa, CO; Rio Grande, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.213ba221d7b769dbc77d0a70fed84b33a31dcfd5.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.213ba221d7b769dbc77d0a70fed84b33a31dcfd5.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-24T19:25:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 241925 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 125 PM MDT Sat Oct 24 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Heavy rain likely to occur over parts of the southeast plains this afternoon into tonight. - Low lying agricultural flooding in the western side of the San Luis Valley likely for the next day or two. - dry weather through next week. - Another impactful storm possi","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-24T17:20:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 241720 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1120 AM MDT Sat Oct 24 2026 COZ058>089-093>099-251730- Western Mosquito Range/East Lake County Above 11000 Feet- Leadville Vicinity/Lake County Below 11000 Feet- Eastern Sawatch Mountains Above 11000 Feet- Western Chaffee County Between 9000 and 11000 Feet- Central Chaffee County Below 9000 Feet- Western Mos","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=HWO&format=CI"},"fwf":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-24T19:49:00+00:00","snippet":".Discussion... Meteorolo